-- 0080: repair the machine/chin classifier collision, curate the movements the
-- selector could not see, and re-ground every citation on a real vault note.
--
-- NOTE ON SHAPE: exercise_science is a VIEW over exercise_muscle (the rows whose
-- citation IS NOT NULL) -- curating a movement means filling the science columns
-- on its existing exercise_muscle row, NOT inserting into the view. Writing to
-- the view fails outright, and a DELETE+INSERT on exercise_muscle would silently
-- destroy any science already curated there. Both are avoided below.
--
-- 1. CLASSIFIER. classify_exercise tested "chin" as a bare substring, which also
--    matches ma-CHIN-e. Seven exercises / 2,155 logged sets were classified as
--    chin-ups: Ab Crunch Machine (744 sets) credited to lats instead of abs, and
--    five overhead-press variants (1,402 sets) credited as PULLING -- which also
--    reset the pull rest-gate clock on a push day, the exact class of miscue
--    ENGINE_INVARIANTS #4 exists to prevent. Fixed in code with a word-boundary
--    helper; the stored rows are repaired here. The DELETE is guarded on
--    citation IS NULL so it can never drop a curated row.
--
-- 2. CURATION. The engine could not select these movements at all -- no science
--    row means never a candidate, never credits a head, never competes for a
--    slot -- despite tens of thousands of logged sets. 59 rows are UPDATEs onto
--    an existing (exercise, muscle) pair; 5 are INSERTs for movements with no
--    muscle row at all. 4 curated rows were deliberately NOT applied because
--    they would CHANGE muscle attribution rather than annotate it (both upright
--    rows traps->front_delts, both sumo squats +adductors). Those are training
--    decisions, not curation, and are left for an explicit call.
--
-- 3. CITATIONS. 113 of 126 curated rows cited a paper appearing nowhere in the
--    vault, against the planner's own rule to cite only real catalogue notes.
--    80 are re-grounded on notes whose CONTENT was read and confirmed to support
--    the specific claim. 33 could not be and are MARKED 'UNGROUNDED: ...' rather
--    than given a citation that would look real and not be -- the row stays
--    usable, the provenance gap stays greppable.
--
-- Every citation written here was verified verbatim against the 804-note vault.

-- ── 1. classifier repair ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DELETE FROM exercise_muscle WHERE exercise_name = 'Machine Shoulder Press' AND citation IS NULL;
INSERT INTO exercise_muscle (exercise_name, muscle, role, credit) SELECT 'Machine Shoulder Press', 'front_delts', 'primary', 1.0 WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM exercise_muscle WHERE exercise_name='Machine Shoulder Press' AND muscle='front_delts');
INSERT INTO exercise_muscle (exercise_name, muscle, role, credit) SELECT 'Machine Shoulder Press', 'side_delts', 'secondary', 0.5 WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM exercise_muscle WHERE exercise_name='Machine Shoulder Press' AND muscle='side_delts');
